+/*
+   A scene is at least as tall as the card it is in.
+ 
+   Lunacy's change. A scene element is the content of Mojo's scene scroller, which is given
+   the card's height; the scene itself is left at its content's height. On a device the
+   scroller is `overflow: -webkit-palm-overflow`, webOS's own scrolling model, and the scene
+   fills it - which is what every `height: 100%` child of a scene depends on. Chromium has no
+   such value, the scroller falls back to `overflow: hidden`, and a scene whose own content is
+   short collapses to nothing: drPodder's splash paints its background with a
+   `position: absolute; height: 100%` div inside the scene, so it came out as a grey card with
+   the logo adrift in it instead of the reference device's full-bleed gradient.
+ 
+   min-height rather than height, so a scene taller than the card still scrolls.
+ */
+.palm-scene {
+  min-height: 100%;
+}
